{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"/*\\n    This program solves Laplace's equation on a regular 2D grid using simple Jacobi iteration.\\n\\n    The stencil calculation stops when  ( err >= CONV_THRESHOLD OR  iter > ITER_MAX )\\n*/\\n#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <time.h>\\n#include <sys/time.h>\\n\\n#define CONV_THRESHOLD 1.0e-5f // threshold of convergence\\n\\n// matrix to be solved\\ndouble **grid;\\n\\n// auxiliary matrix\\ndouble **new_grid;\\n\\n// size of each side of the grid\\nint size;\\nint iter_max_num;\\n\\n// return the absolute value of a number\\ndouble absolute(double num){\\n    if(num < 0)\\n        return -1.0 * num;\\n    return num;\\n}\\n\\n\\n// allocate memory for the grid\\nvoid allocate_memory(){\\n    grid = (double **) malloc(size * sizeof(double *));\\n    new_grid = (double **) malloc(size * sizeof(double *));\\n\\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\\n        grid[i] = (double *) malloc(size * sizeof(double));\\n        new_grid[i] = (double *) malloc(size * sizeof(double));\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// initialize the grid\\nvoid initialize_grid(){\\n    int center = size / 2;\\n    int linf = center - (size / 10);\\n    int lsup = center + (size / 10);\\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++){\\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; j++){\\n            // inicializa região de calor no centro do grid\\n            if ( i >= linf && i <= lsup && j >= linf && j <= lsup)\\n                grid[i][j] = 100;\\n            else\\n                grid[i][j] = 0;\\n            new_grid[i][j] = grid[i][j];\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// save the grid in a file\\nvoid save_grid(){\\n\\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\\n        for(int j = 0; j < size; j++){\\n            fprintf(stdout, \\\"%lf \\\", grid[i][j]);\\n        }\\n        fprintf(stdout, \\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]){\\n\\n    fscanf(stdin, \\\"%d\\\", &size);\\n    fscanf(stdin, \\\"%d\\\", &iter_max_num);\\n    \\n    int hasError = 1;\\n    int iter = 0;\\n    int keepGoing = 1;\\n    int hasComputedIteration = 0;\\n\\n    struct timeval time_start;\\n    struct timeval time_end;\\n\\n    // allocate memory to the grid (matrix)\\n    allocate_memory();\\n\\n    // set grid initial conditions\\n    initialize_grid();\\n\\n    //printf(\\\"Jacobi relaxation calculation: %d x %d grid\\\\n\\\", size, size);\\n\\n    // get the start time\\n    //gettimeofday(&time_start, NULL);\\n\\n    // Jacobi iteration using one team for the complete solve.\\n    #pragma omp parallel if(size >= 64 && iter_max_num > 0) default(none) shared(grid, new_grid, size, iter_max_num, hasError, iter, keepGoing, hasComputedIteration)\\n    {\\n        while (1) {\\n            #pragma omp single\\n            {\\n                if (hasComputedIteration) {\\n                    double **temp_grid = grid;\\n                    grid = new_grid;\\n                    new_grid = temp_grid;\\n                    ++iter;\\n                    hasComputedIteration = 0;\\n                }\\n\\n                keepGoing = hasError && iter < iter_max_num;\\n                if (keepGoing) {\\n                    hasError = 0;\\n                    hasComputedIteration = 1;\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if (!keepGoing)\\n                break;\\n\\n            #pragma omp for schedule(static) reduction(|:hasError)\\n            for (int i = 1; i < size - 1; i++) {\\n                double * restrict new_row = new_grid[i];\\n                const double * restrict current_row = grid[i];\\n                const double * restrict north_row = grid[i - 1];\\n                const double * restrict south_row = grid[i + 1];\\n                int row_has_error = 0;\\n\\n                #pragma omp simd reduction(|:row_has_error)\\n                for (int j = 1; j < size - 1; j++) {\\n                    new_row[j] = 0.25 * (current_row[j + 1] + current_row[j - 1] +\\n                                         north_row[j] + south_row[j]);\\n\\n                    double errorCurrent = absolute(new_row[j] - current_row[j]);\\n                    if (errorCurrent > CONV_THRESHOLD) {\\n                        row_has_error = 1;\\n                    }\\n                }\\n                hasError |= row_has_error;\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    // get the end time\\n    //gettimeofday(&time_end, NULL);\\n\\n    //double exec_time = (double) (time_end.tv_sec - time_start.tv_sec) +\\n    //                   (double) (time_end.tv_usec - time_start.tv_usec) / 1000000.0;\\n\\n    //save the final grid in file\\n    save_grid();\\n\\n    //printf(\\\"\\\\nKernel executed in %lf seconds with %d iterations.\\\\n\\\", exec_time, iter);\\n\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/laplace_seq.c\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"A persistent OpenMP team can reduce per-iteration team-launch overhead; static row worksharing, SIMD convergence reduction, and swapping initialized buffers avoid the copy pass while preserving the stencil and output.\",\"notes\":\"Combines the declared persistent-team, SIMD, restrict-pointer, and buffer-swap ideas. Correctness and performance remain for controller evaluation.\",\"research\":{\"queries\":[],\"urls\":[]},\"sources_kept\":[\"c913d8c7c1b44cd5\",\"2a428b032aae40e0\",\"dd4455f28bcb48ba\"],\"transformations\":[\"Use one conditionally enabled OpenMP parallel region for the iterative solve, with static row worksharing and a bitwise-OR convergence reduction.\",\"Apply an inner SIMD loop with a local bitwise-OR convergence reduction and restrict-qualified row pointers.\",\"Initialize both grids identically and swap their pointers after each completed stencil iteration instead of copying the updated interior.\"]}"}}
